{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794742016,"nonce":"3jRMSxqFKxRTVGk5anLwR+k/72M=","message":"Started in hx-n/hxn-gpu-d3d12 (628fa36, then .gitattributes). windows 0.62; adapters with WARP; buffers in default, upload and readback heaps; textures with an RTV; root signatures of root descriptors from HLSL_SLOTS through sources/ on hxn 0.3.2; compute and graphics PSOs; command lists with resource-state transitions and UAV barriers; execute as an hxn future from a thread waiting on the fence (SetEventOnCompletion with a null event).\n\nCI on windows-latest with WARP: examples/check (compute over 64 ints, a quad into a 4x4 texture copied to a readback buffer, all read back and checked) passes on Ash, stock HashLink, hxcpp and CPPIA, on the first run.\n\nDiffers from the design on 4db10ab: transitions use resource states, not enhanced barriers, which need a newer D3D12 runtime than the CI image is known to have. Not yet: textures and samplers (descriptor tables, the sampler heap and naga's per-group sampler index buffer at space255), DXIL built during the Haxe build with DXC (HLSL is compiled at load by d3dcompiler_47 to SM 5.1), presenting to a window, and the debug layer (the runners lack Graphics Tools).","files":null}]}